{"title":"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A region is bounded by semicircular arcs constructed on the side of a square whose sides measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80c5dddbc62faa2e29515da4b433c4c8dc9613f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" />, as shown. What is the perimeter of this region?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2f7d7427c74567de47a93edfad961d23cd8633.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(90); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); filldraw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle,gray(0.5)); filldraw(arc((1,0),1,180,0, CCW)--cycle,gray(0.7)); filldraw(arc((0,1),1,90,270)--cycle,gray(0.7)); filldraw(arc((1,2),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.7)); filldraw(arc((2,1),1,270,90, CCW)--cycle,gray(0.7)); [/asy]\" width=\"152\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc3ae8fc4036a4e5f1dc1f776ed94cc7763c385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{4}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{8}{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{16}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the side of the square is the diameter of the semicircle, the radius of the semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/0680bee2333595261957a2fd4ddc10f70252932f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{\\pi}=\\frac{1}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since the length of one of the semicircular <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arc\" title=\"Arc\">arcs</a> is half the circumference of the corresponding circle, the length of one arc is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a65f59645830f43b279e8cd97d70691d34e1d1ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot2\\cdot\\pi\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\pi}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Since the desired perimeter is made up of four of these arcs, the perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82f541406ff2ef1e80f69f30c8c17665bb6a916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"114\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B\">2006 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Re